        The root cause of the bug is the continued support for the deprecated `dfs.umask` configuration, which could lead to confusion and incorrect behavior when users attempt to set file permissions using an outdated configuration key. The presence of fallback logic for the old umask value could result in unexpected behavior if the old and new umask values do not match, potentially causing security and permission issues in file handling.

        Commit message:
        HADOOP-12294. Remove the support of the deprecated dfs.umask.
 Contributed by Chang Li.  

